{{also|Dunkel}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|dunkel|lang=gmh}}, {{term|tunkel|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|tunkal|lang=goh}}, {{term|tuncal||dark|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|dunkalaz||dark|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{recons|dʰengw-||to smoke, fume|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with {{etyl|gml|-}} {{term|dunker||dark|lang=gml}} and Dutch ''[[donker]]'' ("dark").

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈdʊŋkl̩/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-at-dunkel.ogg|audio (Austria)}}

===Adjective===
{{de-adj|dunkler|dunkelsten}}

# [[dark]]
#: Im Winter wird es früher '''dunkel'''. &mdash; In the winter, it gets '''dark''' earlier.
#: Das '''[[dunkle]]''' Rot gefällt mir besser. &mdash; I like the '''dark''' red better.

